<article class="env-lemma" id="0CX0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CX0">Lemma <span data-tag="0CX0">77.11.6</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0CWU" data-tag="0CWU">77.11.4</a>. Let $h : X' \to X$ be an étale morphism. Set $\mathcal{F}' = h^*\mathcal{F}$ and $f' = f \circ h$. Let $F_ n'$ be (<a href="/tag/0CWV" data-tag="0CWV">77.11.4.1</a>) associated to $(f' : X' \to Y, \mathcal{F}')$. Then $F_ n$ is a subfunctor of $F_ n'$ and if $h(X') \supset \text{Ass}_{X/Y}(\mathcal{F})$, then $F_ n = F'_ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $U \to X$, $V \to Y$, $U \to V$ as in part (1) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0CWS" data-tag="0CWS">77.11.2</a>. Choose a surjective étale morphism $U' \to U \times _ X X'$ where $U'$ is a scheme. Then we have the lemma for the two functors $F_{U, n}$ and $F_{U', n}$ determined by $U' \to U$ and $\mathcal{F}|_ U$ over $V$, see More on Flatness, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UD" data-tag="05UD">38.27.2</a>. On the other hand, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CWS" data-tag="0CWS">77.11.2</a> tells us that given $T \to Y$ we have $F_ n(T) = F_{U, n}(V \times _ Y T)$ and $F'_ n(T) = F_{U', n}(V \times _ Y T)$. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>